  "narrative": "No assessments are due and voluntary validation is exhausted, so this stage registers corrected discovery-only refinements for the central feature_038 context question. The corrected form avoids using feature_038 simultaneously in eligibility and subgroup: feature_038 appears only in subgroup bands, while eligibility excludes the strongest co-occurring core predictors. The registered comparisons map the feature_038 quartile gradient rather than only the extreme high and low bands. For feature_063, direction -1 means a positive signed estimate corresponds to the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast being negative, i.e. feature_063=1 is associated with lower outcome_001 and stronger composite dependency. The mid-high band proposal tests whether feature_063 association begins to rise before the high quartile; the low-mid band tests whether any threshold-supported effect exists below feature_038=0. For feature_010, direction +1 means a positive signed estimate corresponds to the raw contrast being positive, i.e. feature_010=1 is associated with higher outcome_001 and weaker dependency. The low-mid and mid-high main-effect tests ask where attenuation occurs: is feature_010 strong only in low feature_038, preserved into low-mid but not mid-high, or attenuated across mid-high as in the extreme high band? The additional direction -1 feature_010 mid-high test checks the unlikely reversal pattern in which feature_010=1 would be associated with lower outcome_001 and stronger dependency. The broader interaction tests at feature_038 ge 0 are clean but less local: feature_063 amplification asks whether above-median feature_038 increases the stronger-dependency association relative to its complement; feature_010 attenuation asks whether above-median feature_038 reduces the weaker-dependency association relative to its complement, using direction -1 so that a positive signed interaction indicates raw attenuation. These remain descriptive associations in the supplied dataset, based on post-hoc quartile-like cuts and many correlated subgroup tests. They do not establish causality, biological mechanism, single-gene meaning, or generalizability. If the bands show a monotone feature_063 gradient and progressive feature_010 attenuation, a continuous or prespecified quantile-bin feature_038 modifier model will be more defensible. If only the extreme high feature_038 bands show amplification, the earlier extreme-cut context model should remain the main conclusion and the intermediate gradient should be treated as unsupported.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 22 explore corrected registration. No assessments due; validation budget exhausted. Current supported core: feature_037=1 stronger dependency, feature_002=1 weaker dependency, overall feature_010=1 weaker dependency but attenuated in high feature_038, and feature_063=1 stronger dependency especially in high feature_038. Main unresolved issue is whether feature_038 acts as a threshold gate or graded modifier. Registered seven discovery claims using feature_038 only in subgroup and eligibility for distinct core-predictor exclusions. They test feature_063 in low-mid and mid-high feature_038 bands, feature_010 in low-mid and mid-high bands, a mid-high feature_010 reversal direction, and broader above-median feature_038 interactions for feature_063 amplification and feature_010 attenuation. Interpretation conventions: negative-direction feature_063/feature_010 claims: positive signed means raw negative, i.e. stronger dependency. Positive-direction feature_010: positive signed means raw positive, i.e. weaker dependency. Negative-direction feature_010 attenuation interactions: positive signed means raw interaction is negative/attenuated in the subgroup. If these intermediate bands reproduce the high-vs-low gradient, the feature_038 modifier model is strengthened; if only extremes differ, retain extreme-cut feature_038 context and avoid inferring a continuous gradient. All conclusions remain supplied-dataset associations only."
